A||N||2||terryk||Difference in Federal and California V6 Proms||||1||
Z||000000||terryk||10-01-2001||12:00 AM||||Someone asked me about this. I can't remember the thread. I another thread I said I'd look. <P>I compared two sets.<P>4 spd V6 CA and Fed<BR>5 spd V6 CA and Fed<P>The difference:<BR>Prom ID (expected)<BR>Checksum (expected)<BR>Cold Engine AFR MAP vs CTS is run .1 richer for CA in the 90F coolant range. No real difference for all intents and purposes.<P>So, they are the essentially the same.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jefrysuko||10-01-2001||02:03 AM||||I believe that it was me that you were doing that for.  I would have thought there would be more of a difference than that.  It makes you wonder why they even bothered.  Thank you.<BR>Jeffrey<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||10-01-2001||02:21 AM||||I think that since CA has "different" standards, the auto companies feel compelled to make a different chip. <P>There are others that have similar non-differences. On the 92/93 SC, in CA you can't downshift to 1st until you below 31 MPH vs federal's 35 MPH. Only difference.<P>TK||||reg||1
